Using the stringent limit on the source luminosity together with detections and limits on the detection of the source obtained at other times we have constructed the long term X-ray lightcurve of 1H 1905+000 (see Fig. 2)5. From Fig. 2 it is clear that the source underwent an outburst with a duration of at least 9.9 years (the time between the first and last detection). Using the SAS-3 satellite several type I X-ray bursts were detected (Li et al. 1976 [multiple bursts], Lewin et al. 1976b , Lewin et al. 1976a ). However, since the persistent flux level was in most cases not quoted only 1 SAS-3 point appears in Fig. 2.

